---
import Icon from "./Icon.astro";
---

<section class="sec" id="install">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="rv">
      <div class="label">Local first</div>
      <h2 class="h2">Your code stays on your machine.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="priv rv">
      <div>
        <h3>Your tools, your sign-ins</h3>
        <p>
          Otaq runs the real <span class="mono">claude</span>, <span class="mono">codex</span>,{" "}
          <span class="mono">copilot</span> and <span class="mono">opencode</span> programs with your own
          subscriptions and permission modes. Never your passwords or keys.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>No account, no server</h3>
        <p>
          Tickets live in <span class="mono">~/.otaq</span>. Worktrees sit outside your repository, one per
          ticket. Pushes happen only at a Delivery stage you set.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Otaq itself sends nothing</h3>
        <p>
          Unless you opt in to anonymous usage data: which features are used, the Otaq version and your OS.
          Never code, ticket text or file names. There is no update check.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="status rv">
      <div>
        <h3>
          <span class="pill p-pa">
            <Icon icon="info" />
            v0.1
          </span>
          Honest status
        </h3>
        <p>
          Otaq is used daily by its author and is early. There are no prebuilt releases yet: build it from
          source. macOS is the most tested platform; Windows and Linux build and run but have seen less use.
          Expect rough edges, and please open issues.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Build from source</h3>
        <p>Rust 1.99+ and Node 24, plus at least one agent tool installed and signed in.</p>
        <div class="term">
          <div>
            <span class="c"># the desktop app (the web page is built into the binary)</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="g">$</span> git clone https://github.com/otaq-io/otaq.git &amp;&amp; cd otaq
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="g">$</span> cd crates/otaq-desktop &amp;&amp; npm ci &amp;&amp; npm run tauri build
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="c">
              # the otaq command: opens the app, runs the service, and is what agents call
            </span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="g">$</span> cargo build --release -p otaq-cli
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="g">$</span> otaq
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
